; Reproducer for the infinite loop in the backend's `insert_ref_distances`
; (see README.md in this directory, issue 5).
;
; `v0` is received by the first instruction and consumed by the last one,
; 1025 reference units later: each `iconst.i32 0x12345678` is emitted as a
; `const` plus three `grow`s (4 units) and each `iadd` is one unit, and
; there are 205 pairs. An `echo.l` reference can express at most 1023, and
; the pass bridges the distance by inserting an `echo.l` right after the
; definition, which leaves the remaining distance unchanged, so it inserts
; echoes forever:
;
;   llvm2clif far_reference_1025.clif -o out.o    # never finishes
;
; `far_reference_1020.clif` is the same function with one pair less
; (reference distance 1020) and compiles in about 10 ms.

